#189 still isn't done: no nightly has yet shown a fresh security report for any of the eight repositories. #210 has merged, but the nightlies don't run its code yet. This run changed no code; it backs off until 2026-11-23 10:00Z, after today's repository scans.

- **What the nightlies run:** image cd7d3689 (since cloud#82). It has this issue's CodeQL memory sizing (the `--ram`/`--threads` change) but not #210's change. That change makes a security job that leaves no findings publish a "no report" summary, so a nightly that runs out of memory without publishing becomes visible.
- **What gets #210 there:** two more steps. looper#221 has to pin an image that includes #210's commit, cc25fdf, and then cloud#92 has to point tacplus-dev/build at it. looper#221 isn't approved yet and asks only for a pin at or after d8e72ad. I commented there asking for a pin at or after cc25fdf.
- **Next run:** it reads the 2026-11-23 nightly's security summaries for eventbus, stratum, mailbox, llmproxy, redo, kernel, tenantecho and messaging as the repository scans quote them. If they're fresh, have no CodeQL out-of-memory problem and their memory peaks are under 12Gi, it posts the outcome comment and closes #189. If they're still stale, it records `Blocked-by: #221`.
- **Unconfirmed guess for the stale reports:** on 2026-11-21 and 2026-11-22 the tenantecho and messaging security jobs published nothing. One possible cause is that a pod asking for 12Gi never gets scheduled on the build nodes. I can't check that without access to tacplus-dev/build. It's in the checkpoint, so whatever summary shows up next gets checked for it.

The checkpoint pushed "2 files changed, 861 insertions" to the `looper/looper-189` branch even though my checkout showed nothing uncommitted. I didn't check what those files were.
